// Type-check the plain-JavaScript board code (lib/board/*.js), which the main
// tsconfig deliberately does NOT include — adding it there would fail
// `next build`. This config is opt-in and emits nothing.
//
// RUN IT WITH:
//   npm run typecheck:js        the raw list (expect ~420 errors — see below)
//   npm run ratchet             the CI gate: fails only if that number went UP
//                               (the authoritative current number lives in
//                                scripts/baselines/quality-baseline.json)
//
// IT IS NO LONGER A DEAD FILE. As of the CI work, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
// runs `npm run ratchet`, which re-counts these errors on every push and
// compares the total against the number committed in
// `scripts/baselines/quality-baseline.json`.
//
//   count goes UP    → CI fails. Your change added a new loose-DOM error.
//   count goes DOWN  → CI passes and lowers the committed baseline, so the
//                      ceiling is permanently reduced and can never drift back.
//
// So: the errors here are a to-fix list, not a build gate, exactly as before —
// but the list can now only get shorter. You are never asked to fix the ~420;
// you are asked not to add one more. Full explanation of the mechanism is in
// the header of scripts/ratchet.mjs.
//
// Why the errors exist: lib/board/*.js was ported near-verbatim from
// prototype_1.html and does untyped DOM work throughout — `el.value` on an
// `HTMLElement`, properties hung off `window`, object literals grown at
// runtime. Each one is individually harmless and collectively a real risk.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "incremental": false,
    "strict": false,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["lib/board/*.js"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
